## 3. Review Findings and Suggested Improvements

### QR-V2-011-I01 — Positive Review Findings

**Finding 1: Clear project purpose and learning direction**

Section 1 explains that the project aims to introduce Artificial Intelligence to first-year university students and beginners without a technical background.

The document also establishes the three main learning resources and the Live Mini Lecture as the project's intended outputs.

**Finding 2: Detailed shared Markdown content**

Section 2 provides chapter-by-chapter descriptions of the five original Stage 1 chapters. The descriptions explain the topics, learning activities and intended educational value of each chapter.

The document also explains how shared Markdown content serves as the foundation for the other learning resources.

**Finding 3: Clear chapter development records**

Section 3 provides a development-status overview with verification dates and remaining-work information.

The Chapter 3 numbering decision is also documented, including the correction record and confirmation that the table-of-contents links were checked.

**Finding 4: Appropriate Stage 1 focus topic selection**

The selection of Chapter 5 Topic 1: Bias is supported by a dedicated record.

The required-element table documents explanations, terminology, a worked example, a visual, a learner activity, an answer key and references.

This makes the selection process understandable and traceable.

**Finding 5: Comprehensive Study Guide and Test Bank planning**

Section 4 explains how the chapters will be adapted into independent learning materials and assessment questions.

It includes different question types and emphasises understanding and application rather than memorisation alone.

**Finding 6: Detailed PPT Slides planning**

Section 5 provides a chapter-based presentation plan.

It identifies important concepts, comparisons, examples, diagrams and activities that can be adapted into slides while preserving the original Markdown content.

**Finding 7: Clear Video Tutorials planning**

Section 6 provides a structured tutorial plan for each chapter.

The plan explains how narration, diagrams, demonstrations and short activities can support learners' understanding.

**Finding 8: Meaningful Live Mini Lecture topic**

Section 7 selects the topic "How Can AI Learn to Recognize Spam Emails?"

The topic connects familiar email experiences with machine learning, training data, inference and prediction errors.

The proposed lecture structure also includes audience participation.

**Finding 9: Good integration between learning resources**

Section 8 explains the different roles of the Study Guide and Test Bank, PPT Slides and Video Tutorials.

The document also describes how learners can use the resources together as part of a coherent learning experience.

**Finding 10: Complete Stage 1 submission documentation**

Section 9 includes the required submission package, checklist, package record and peer-review record.

The checklist provides a clear way to track the existence and verification of required submission materials.

**Finding 11: Defined team responsibilities**

Section 10 assigns responsibilities to all five team members.

The role descriptions establish ownership for content development, visual design, quality review, video production and project coordination.

**Finding 12: Repository evidence and contribution tracking**

Section 11 documents the types of repository evidence required and provides an individual contribution map.

This helps connect project participation with actual files, sections and development activities.

**Finding 13: AI-use documentation**

Section 12 explains how significant AI assistance should be recorded and verified.

It also distinguishes shared project AI-use records from individual personal logs, supporting clearer documentation of AI-assisted work.

**Finding 14: Documented timeline and workflow**

Section 13 presents the three project stages, internal deadlines and official deadlines.

The workflow provides a logical sequence from research and drafting to review, resource production and final submission.

**Finding 15: Quality assurance and risk management**

Section 14 identifies potential project challenges and describes practical measures for maintaining accuracy, consistency, evidence and timely completion.

**Finding 16: Quality review response tracking**

Section 15 records the responses to QR-007-I01, QR-007-I02 and QR-007-I03.

The response summary, feedback communication record and review history provide a traceable record of earlier quality-review activities.

